In broadcastWizardLogic.ts: `const existingSchedules = await hogFlowsSchedulesList(projectId, broadcastId)
await Promise.all(
    existingSchedules.map((existingSchedule) =>
        hogFlowsSchedulesDestroy(projectId, broadcastId, existingSchedule.id)
    )
)` and `if (values.scheduleMode === 'now') {
    await hogFlowsBatchJobsCreate(projectId, broadcastId, {
        hog_flow: broadcastId,
    })
    lemonToast.success('Broadcast sent')
} else {
    // ...
    await hogFlowsSchedulesCreate(projectId, broadcastId, schedule as any)
    lemonToast.success('Broadcast scheduled')
}`.

In broadcastWizardLogic.ts, the broadcast is marked active before schedule replacement finishes: `activated = await hogFlowsPartialUpdate(projectId, broadcastId, { status: 'active' })

// Replace any existing schedule with a fresh, active one so a relaunched
// broadcast always sends at the chosen time and never ends up silently paused.
const existingSchedules = await hogFlowsSchedulesList(projectId, broadcastId)`.

In BroadcastSummary.tsx: `<LemonButton
    type="secondary"
    size="small"
    onClick={moveToDraft}
    loading={movingToDraft}
    data-attr="broadcast-move-to-draft"
>
    Move to draft
</LemonButton>` and in broadcastWizardLogic.ts: `moveToDraft: async () => {
    if (!values.currentProjectId || !values.broadcastId) {
        actions.moveToDraftFinished()
        return
    }
    const projectId = String(values.currentProjectId)
    const broadcastId = values.broadcastId
    try {
        const updated = await hogFlowsPartialUpdate(projectId, broadcastId, { status: 'draft' })`. The action triggers directly without any confirmation step.

In broadcastWizardLogic.ts: `try {
    const updated = await hogFlowsPartialUpdate(projectId, broadcastId, { status: 'draft' })
    actions.saveBroadcastFinished(updated)
    actions.hydrateFromBroadcast(updated)
    lemonToast.success('Broadcast moved to draft')
} catch (error: any) {
    lemonToast.error(
        `Couldn't move the broadcast to draft: ${error?.detail || error?.message || 'unknown error'}`
    )
} finally {
    actions.moveToDraftFinished()
}`. Existing send runs are not cancelled and no run cancellation status warnings are handled.

In broadcastWizardLogic.ts, existing schedules are deleted without reading variable overrides: `await Promise.all(
    existingSchedules.map((existingSchedule) =>
        hogFlowsSchedulesDestroy(projectId, broadcastId, existingSchedule.id)
    )
)` and the new schedule is created solely from wizard values: `await hogFlowsSchedulesCreate(projectId, broadcastId, schedule as any)`.
